    <string name="zip_guide_title">Load games from a ROM ZIP</string>
    <string name="zip_guide_summary">One ZIP, every game. Retrobit unpacks it and files each game under its console.</string>
    <string name="zip_guide_open">Step-by-step guide</string>
    <string name="zip_guide_close">Close</string>
    <string name="zip_guide_step1">1. Put all your ROMs in one ZIP file (for example ROMS.zip). Subfolders such as GBA or SNES are fine.</string>
    <string name="zip_guide_step2">2. Open a file manager (File Manager Plus works well on TV boxes).</string>
    <string name="zip_guide_step3">3. Tap “Select ROM ZIP” in Retrobit.</string>
    <string name="zip_guide_step4">4. Find the ZIP and confirm access. Retrobit only reads the file you pick.</string>
    <string name="zip_guide_step5">5. Retrobit opens the ZIP and adds every game to its console automatically.</string>
    <string name="zip_guide_note">Use this button for ZIP or 7z archives. To add individual ROMs, choose the import files button.</string>
    <string name="zip_guide_formats_title">Supported formats</string>
    <string name="zip_guide_limits">ZIPs over 1 GB can take much longer. Keep Retrobit open and the screen on until it finishes.</string>
